    "result_text": "The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode de-duplication in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**What changed:**\n- The owner-creation path previously assigned `customerCodeFor(owner)` directly (line 178). That code is `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, derived only from the owner's region + telephone/lastName hash, so two distinct owners could in principle collide.\n- Line 178 now wraps that call: `owner.setCustomerCode(deduplicateCustomerCode(customerCodeFor(owner)))`.\n- Added a `deduplicateCustomerCode(String)` helper: it collects all existing owners' customer codes; if the computed code is unused it returns it unchanged, otherwise it appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n >= 2` that produces a code no existing owner holds.\n\nThe suffix keeps the existing format compatible \u2014 `getLocality()` reads the REGION segment before the *first* dash (unaffected) and `getMembershipNumber()` appends `-M<YY>` after the whole code (still valid).\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreCustomerCodesStayUnique`) passes: distinct owners get distinct customer codes.",
